        "date": "2026-11-08T20:42:38Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(setup): align the part to a setup's own frame, separate from the work offset\n\nA setup can hold the part flipped or turned: SetupDef.part_alignment, a\nrigid transform document -> setup frame (None = as modelled), set by the\nundoable AlignPartToSetup (any rigid transform, presets, or typed X/Y/Z\nangles about the parts' centre). Only parts read through it; the setup's\nstock, offsets and fixtures already live in the setup frame. The work\noffset (setup::wcs_slot) is untouched; rotated offsets stay refused.\n\n- The following stock is rebuilt square to the setup frame; a cylinder\n  that would lie down or a shared stock is refused by name. MoveModel\n  conjugates the move for an aligned setup's stock; a datum transfer\n  carries the alignment.\n- Generation (material, model/selection heights), stamps, the program\n  sim's part, stock fit, stock from model and the viewport's drawing and\n  picks read in the setup frame. As modelled every read is the old call,\n  so paths, stamps and posts are byte-identical.\n- In an aligned setup only Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive on\n  a whole model or the stock generate; other kinds, picks, area controls,\n  tilts and non-mill machines are refused by name at collect_job. The\n  program sim refuses a program spanning differently-held setups.\n- Project v53: setup.part_alignment; absent = as modelled (v52 files load\n  unchanged); a non-rigid transform is corrupt.\n- Setups page: Part alignment combo plus typed angles (AlignPart).\n\nFixes #326\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
