      "message": "fix(setup): work-offset anchors read the part in the active setup's frame\n\nThe pane's \"model bounds\" anchors (interact::anchor_reference) read the\ndocument-frame solid bounds, so in an aligned setup a turned part's G54\ncould land on a corner that is not the one on the table. They now read\nsetup_align::solid_aabb_in for the active setup (the setup SetWcs places\noffsets in, and the frame the viewport draws), and the stock anchors read\nthat setup's own stock. An as-modelled setup reads exactly as before.\n\nAlso from the PR #341 review: the setup sheet prints a PART ALIGNMENT\nline when the setup holds the part flipped or turned (nothing as\nmodelled); the alignment words move to setup_align::describe so the page\nand the sheet say the same thing; the part_facets refusal loses its stray\nrun of spaces.\n\nPinned by model_bounds_anchors_follow_the_aligned_part (ui) and\nthe_setup_sheet_names_the_part_alignment (app setup_align).\n\nRefs #326\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
